WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.720
Before the walkthrough, here is how you get LeafLedger. On getleafledger.com, click Start free month. Checkout is handled by Stripe. A card is required, nothing is charged for thirty days, and you can cancel before then from your billing page.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:31.450
After checkout you land on your welcome page. It shows your license key and the download link. Keep the key somewhere safe; it is also kept with your subscription.

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:43.720
Run the installer once, and a LeafLedger icon appears on your desktop. The first time it opens, read the one-time agreement, tick the box, and click I agree.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:56.350
Paste your license key and click Activate, then name your workspace folder. The key is the only thing LeafLedger ever sends anywhere. Now the walkthrough begins.

00:00:56.650 --> 00:01:02.542
Welcome to LeafLedger. This walkthrough uses real application screens and fictional

00:01:02.542 --> 00:01:08.434
practice records for two made-up companies, Riverbend Tobacco Works and Harbor Leaf

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:14.751
Imports. Nothing here is a real business, and nothing you see is submitted to any agency.

00:01:14.751 --> 00:01:21.069
LeafLedger runs on your own computer, and your records stay there. The overview shows the

00:01:21.069 --> 00:01:26.890
four steps of every month: complete setup, add the month's files, prepare, review.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:34.980
Setup is where you describe the business exactly as TTB and FDA know it. The practice

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:41.212
workspace is already filled in: the companies, each permit with its number, the product

00:01:41.212 --> 00:01:47.589
classes each permit reports, and the products with their units. For your own business you

00:01:47.589 --> 00:01:53.320
enter this once. LeafLedger never fills in a fact it cannot verify; it asks you.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:02:01.144
Next, the source file layouts tell LeafLedger which column in your monthly export holds

00:02:01.144 --> 00:02:06.969
which fact. You can use the standard column names, or type the headings your own system

00:02:06.969 --> 00:02:12.927
produces. Below that, the account mapping links every value in your Account column to one

00:02:12.927 --> 00:02:18.684
reporting transaction type. An account that is not mapped stops the month. It is never

00:02:18.684 --> 00:02:19.220
guessed.

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:27.788
Open Monthly cycle, type the reporting month, here August 2026, and click Load month. Each

00:02:27.788 --> 00:02:34.209
month has its own source files and its own results, and nothing from an earlier month is

00:02:34.209 --> 00:02:35.450
ever overwritten.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:42.760
Add the month's export files. In the practice set, that is one file from the

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:48.698
manufacturer's records and one from the importer's, chosen with the matching profile.

00:02:48.698 --> 00:02:54.706
LeafLedger stores each file exactly as supplied and records its fingerprint, so a file

00:02:54.706 --> 00:02:57.920
that changes later can never be used silently.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:06.071
Click Prepare this month. LeafLedger reads every row, checks every captured regulation,

00:03:06.071 --> 00:03:12.080
and renders the draft forms. On the first month there is no earlier filing to compare

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:17.948
against; from the second month on, last month's filing is selected automatically so

00:03:17.948 --> 00:03:22.190
opening stock is checked against the previous closing stock.

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:30.410
Each preparation is archived with a time stamp and a result. The practice month comes back

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:36.491
as Review required. That is the normal outcome: the numbers reconcile, and LeafLedger is

00:03:36.491 --> 00:03:39.670
telling you what still needs a human decision.

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:48.407
Review and export shows two things side by side. Numbers reconciled means every row added

00:03:48.407 --> 00:03:54.916
up, with zero blocking exceptions. Month, review required, means something still needs

00:03:54.916 --> 00:04:01.729
your attention. The open items below each say what to do: here, the official copies of the

00:04:01.729 --> 00:04:07.330
forms are not yet among the evidence. LeafLedger flags; it does not guess.

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:15.807
Further down are the draft forms, line by line. Line 7.d, the opening stock, is 100,000

00:04:15.807 --> 00:04:22.359
sticks, and beside it LeafLedger names the source rows that produced it. Every number on

00:04:22.359 --> 00:04:29.060
every form traces back to your own records. Zero lines are folded away so you can read the

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:30.400
lines that matter.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:39.218
Each form is also rendered as a PDF on the official template, with the certification left

00:04:39.218 --> 00:04:45.884
blank. While anything is unresolved, the copy is stamped as a draft. You review it, you

00:04:45.884 --> 00:04:51.170
sign it, you file it. LeafLedger never files anything on your behalf.

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:58.760
At the bottom of the review page is the reviewed copies card. When nothing is left

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:04.758
unresolved, you enter your name and mark the month reviewed, and LeafLedger writes clean

00:05:04.758 --> 00:05:10.825
copies without the draft stamp, still unsigned. Until then, the card explains exactly why

00:05:10.825 --> 00:05:16.687
the button is not there yet: each open item, and what to do about it. A clean copy can

00:05:16.687 --> 00:05:19.550
never exist for a month with an open item.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:27.802
History lists every preparation ever made. Corrections are recorded as new versions that

00:05:27.802 --> 00:05:34.055
supersede the old ones; nothing is deleted, so you can always show what you prepared and

00:05:34.055 --> 00:05:34.410
when.

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:43.111
Finally, create an encrypted backup with a passphrase you choose. The passphrase is never

00:05:43.111 --> 00:05:49.736
stored, so keep it safe. That is the whole routine: setup once, then every month add the

00:05:49.736 --> 00:05:53.350
files, prepare, and review. Thanks for watching.
